The storage axis
description: where a value lives, and what language it speaks
- >
  The storage concrete answers *where, in what language*: inline in an enclosing document, a
  whole file of its own, opaque bytes, or a directory. Two rules govern the axis. The
  **language-switch rule**: yamlover can switch to json5p mid-stream and yaml to json - never
  the reverse; after a switch, descendants take the switched language. And the **per-node
  rule**: every materialized node carries exactly one concrete, derived from the filesystem
  when unstated. See the subchapters below - the directory story lives in the yamlover
  section, referenced here:
- *: 00-inlined
- *: 01-files
- *: 02-binary_files
- *..:03-yamlover:01-dir
- *: 04-multi_document_streams
